<Ui>
    <!--
        The KEY BINDINGS window (decision 0997) — the era-shaped standalone KeyBindingFrame the
        game menu's Key Bindings button opens, over the engine's binding table
        (benilla_ui::script::keybind + crate::bindings — GetNumBindings/GetBinding/SetBinding/
        GetBindingKey/GetBindingAction/LoadBindings/SaveBindings/GetCurrentBindingSet, the 1.12
        Lua API verbatim). Rows are the HONEST TREE: only commands the engine really dispatches
        are registered, so only they (and only their non-empty categories) appear.

        PROVENANCE (0985 — the three-source split; OptionsFrame.xml carries the sibling block):
        · STRUCTURE & BEHAVIOR — the era Blizzard_BindingUI (wow-ui-source-era @ 1.15.9.68940,
          Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_BindingUI — shipped there though 1.15's Settings supersedes
          it; per 0985's per-window rule the newest classic-dialog form of THIS window is the
          1.13/1.14 one, and that source IS this file's blueprint, the director's own screenshot):
          858x660 CENTER dialog, the 175-wide category sidebar replacing 1.12's inline headers
          (only non-empty categories appear), the bordered bindings container, Command/Key 1/
          Key 2 columns over 25-tall rows, the top-right Character Specific checkbox, and the
          Reset To Default / Unbind Key / Okay / Cancel row. Behavior deltas the era added and
          this file keeps: Reset To Default confirms first; checkbox-kit click sounds.
        · CAPTURE & SET LAW — 1.12's own Blizzard_BindingUI (extracted from patch.MPQ this
          session, `_extracted_addons/`), which the era Lua descends from line-for-line: click a
          key capsule to arm it; the next key or mouse-3/4/5 press binds IMMEDIATELY (the host's
          capture seam hands the canonical ALT-CTRL-SHIFT chord to KeyBindingFrame_OnHostKey);
          a stolen key names its victim in red (KEY_UNBOUND_ERROR); left/right clicks select/
          deselect, never bind; lone modifiers are ignored; the wheel binds click-commands but
          refuses press+release ones (SetBinding returns nil - KEYBINDINGFRAME_MOUSEWHEEL_ERROR);
          binds take effect LIVE; Okay saves (SaveBindings), Cancel/ESC reverts
          (LoadBindings(GetCurrentBindingSet())); the character-specific set is real 1.12
          (DEFAULT/ACCOUNT/CHARACTER = 0/1/2, both confirm popups).
        · ART BYTES — the 1.12 MPQ chain only (0978/0985): the same dialog chrome as
          OptionsFrame.xml (BACKDROP_DIALOG_32_32 recipe: tiled UI-DialogBox-Background at its
          uniform black-60% + the UI-DialogBox-Border rope; UI-DialogBox-Header title plate),
          the tooltip-border OUTLINE boxes, the QuestLogTitleHighlight category wash law, the
          UI-Panel-Button four-state red buttons, the UI-CheckBox set, the shared scroll kit.
          The era's key capsules are UIMenuButtonStretchTemplate over UI-Silver-Button-* —
          VERIFIED ABSENT from the 1.12 chain — so the capsules wear what 1.12's OWN binding
          window wore: UIPanelButtonTemplate2's panel-button art (the selected state is the
          1.12 window's own LockHighlight glow, not the era's silver overlay).
        All strings are the 1.12 GlobalStrings globals (the VM executes the real file at boot):
        KEY_BINDINGS, COMMAND/KEY1/KEY2, NOT_BOUND, BIND_KEY_TO_COMMAND, KEY_BOUND,
        KEY_UNBOUND_ERROR, RESET_TO_DEFAULT, UNBIND, CHARACTER_SPECIFIC_KEYBINDINGS(+TOOLTIP),
        CHARACTER_KEY_BINDINGS, CONFIRM_LOSE_BINDING_CHANGES,
        CONFIRM_DELETING_CHARACTER_SPECIFIC_BINDINGS, KEYBINDINGFRAME_MOUSEWHEEL_ERROR, the
        BINDING_HEADER_*/BINDING_NAME_* row text and the KEY_* key display names — each read
        through a `getglobal(...) or raw` fallback (the era's own `_G[category] or category`
        posture), so a headless test without GlobalStrings still renders raw tokens.
        The era's CONFIRM_RESET_KEYBINDINGS string is 2.x-era text absent from 1.12
        GlobalStrings; the fallback literal below carries it (structure kept, string ours).

        SCOPE / divergences (noted, not bugs):
        - 20 display rows, not the era's 21: the -52 box top (the title plate's clearance, the
          options window's own band) plus the column-label band leaves 500 units of row run.
        - No push-to-talk row, no gamepad arm, no quick-keybind mode (era furniture with no
          benilla mechanism).
        - ESC while a capsule is armed BINDS Escape — 1.12's own law (its OnKeyDown has no
          ESCAPE filter while selected); ESC with nothing armed cancels and closes through the
          shared ladder (UiPanels.xml), reopening the game menu (both references' OnHide).
    -->

